# MiniTool HQ — Spec accuracy gate (format / size / limits)

Applies to any tool or guide that **converts formats**, **resizes images**, or **checks platform dimensions / weight / carton limits** (e.g. HEIC→JPG, Marketplace Image Prep, FBA box checker, future compress/WebP).

## Hard rule

**Do not ship** defaults, presets, Pass/Fail logic, or guide “requirements” tables until a **bidirectional check** is written into the tool’s `docs/specs/NN-*.md`.

### Bidirectional check (both required)

1. **Official source** — Seller Central / Help / Help Center / developer docs for that platform (Amazon, Etsy, TikTok Shop, etc.). Record URL + date reviewed + the numbers you will implement (px, aspect, MB, L×W×H, lb/kg, formats).
2. **Core SERP competitors** — top 3–5 tools or ranking guides for the same job. Note their defaults and where they differ from official.

Then **reconcile**:

| Outcome | Action |
|---------|--------|
| Official clear | Tool defaults **follow official**; copy may say “confirm in Seller Central” |
| Official vague / conflict | Prefer official range; document ambiguity in spec; UI disclaimer |
| Competitor-only number, no official basis | **Do not** present as a hard platform rule |
| Our output must meet claim | E2E or manual check that exported files hit stated size/format (e.g. JPEG, square px, under max MB) |

## Spec block (mandatory in `docs/specs/`)

```markdown
## Spec accuracy (bidirectional)

| Platform / claim | Official source (URL + date) | Competitor check | Our v1 default | Notes |
|------------------|------------------------------|------------------|----------------|-------|
| … | … | … | … | … |

Acceptance: output format/size/limits match the “Our v1 default” column; disclaimer if rules change.
```

## Do / Don’t

- Do: ship seller-safe defaults that match official guidance where known  
- Do: re-check when editing presets or publishing a new marketplace row  
- Don’t: invent “Amazon requires X” from a random blog alone  
- Don’t: mark shipped if format/size claims are unverified against this gate  

